          "general_description": "ARC-AGI-2 assesses AI performance on coloured-grid problems requiring a rule to be inferred from worked examples and applied to new inputs. The release includes 1,000 development problems and three evaluation sets of 120 problems, distinguished by access. This review concerns public test problems, official scoring software and ARC Prize's applicable verified-evaluation rules. Each input permits two attempts, with credit requiring an exact grid match. Scores are averaged first within problems and then across problems. Human solving results informed selection and difficulty matching of evaluation sets. Verified evaluations prescribe settings and spending limits and use one run. Public materials permit inspection, while hidden materials have additional access controls. No AI norms or separately validated skill scales are described. Broader reasoning interpretations are proposed, but supplied studies concern grid problems."
        },
        "part_B": {
          "information_sources": "Only the supplied benchmark passage and EFPA extraction. Referenced software, reports and archives were not independently inspected. No confidential publisher material was supplied.",
